Both types are opaque in the public headers. C allocates and initializes them, retains no key pointer, and frees them through the `av_malloc` family. I’ll use `ffibox` owners and borrowed handles, keeping the private fields hidden. AES key lengths will be checked before C is called: a failed C initializer can otherwise leave an existing context unusable.
